 "_doc": "College of the Atlantic pier as it stands (Matt's 3 Nov photos matt_3nov_coa_pier_caisson, _head_ledge; site 1 rows 2.30-2.37): a teal steel pony truss on a concrete abutment and a sheet-pile cell, then the aluminium gangway and floats (unchanged, tools/coa_pier.py). The 19 Oct build called it a timber pier on piles; it never was. Numbers from the 2021 lidar, along the OSM line from (-1598.0, 470.2): deck +4.82, top chord +5.95, 2.2 m between trusses, s -1.4 to 35; the cell's head returns +3.73..4.00, a circle fitted to 40 returns centre s 33.13 o 0.08, r 1.86. Panels (12) counted in the caisson photo. ASSUMED: abutment's foot, cell's bed, the lights, what the cables run to.",
